  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces_ast_fixture",
    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces: a minimal consuming model binding NLEV=8 at the import edge, writing du/dt = -D(F, wrt: lev) for a declared interface flux F (shape [lev_nodes]). The plain-D match must fire through the fixpoint (priority 0, where F: [lev_nodes]) and lower to the rule's single-region makearray over [1,8] holding the imported flux-difference aggregate (F[k+1]-F[k])/dz[k]. The model follows the grid's EDGE-ARRAY contract at NLEV=8: it supplies the 9-interface (lev_nodes) quadratic-stretch array ze and derives zc = column_cell_center(ze), dz = column_cell_thickness(ze), all spelled with the literal 8 because the edge binding closes NLEV. The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST -- including the grid-derived geometry observeds -- across bindings.",
